<td id="A4.T15.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:369.9pt;"><span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_align_left undefined">\Block</span>
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">[l]<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Time]</span> 2012-10-28 13:18:40, Sunday 
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Location]</span> City Park 
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Life Event]</span> On a breezy Sunday afternoon at the city park, I went for a short jog as cross<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>training between studio days. While navigating a patch of uneven gravel, I lightly twisted my right ankle and felt mild pain. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Explicit Intention]</span> 
- Seeks quick remedies to alleviate current ankle discomfort. 
- Wants guidance on modifying running techniques for better safety on uneven terrain. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.2.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Implicit Intention]</span> 
- Aims to understand methods to prevent similar ankle injuries while jogging in the future.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T15.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T15.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A4.T15.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:0.0pt;"><span id="A4.T15.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_align_left undefined">\RowStyle</span>
<span id="A4.T15.2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">[nb-rows=1,rowcolor=gray!15]
<span id="A4.T15.2.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Block</span>[l]1-2<span id="A4.T15.2.3.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 2</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T15.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T15.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T15.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="A4.T15.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:369.9pt;"><span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_align_left undefined">\Block</span>
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">[l]<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Time]</span> 2012-05-16 17:42:44, Wednesday 
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Location]</span> Arts &amp; Crafts Store 
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Life Event]</span> In a downtown arts<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>and<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>crafts store with rain pattering outside, I’m choosing simple decor for my apartment, but the wall of options makes my chest tighten and my thoughts stall. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Explicit Intention]</span> 
- Seeks a quick technique to alleviate stress and indecision while shopping. 
- Desires improved focus to make decisions efficiently despite distractions. 
- Wants a practical exercise that fits into a succinct, no-fluff lifestyle. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.4.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Implicit Intention]</span> 
- Aims to regain emotional calm amid overwhelming choices in a public setting. 
- Hopes to feel at ease adjusting to environmental factors like rain during outings.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T15.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T15.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A4.T15.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:0.0pt;"><span id="A4.T15.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_align_left undefined">\RowStyle</span>
<span id="A4.T15.2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">[nb-rows=1,rowcolor=gray!15]
<span id="A4.T15.2.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Block</span>[l]1-2<span id="A4.T15.2.5.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 3</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T15.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T15.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T15.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"></td>
<td id="A4.T15.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:369.9pt;"><span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_align_left undefined">\Block</span>
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">[l]<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Time]</span> 2012-07-07 19:15:05, Saturday 
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Location]</span> Video Store 
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Life Event]</span> On a rainy Saturday evening, while idly waiting in the quiet aisle of a downtown video<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>rental shop, he pulls out his phone and watches a short social<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>media clip that outlines the dangers of eating fast food every day, which spikes his anxiety about his own eating patterns. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Explicit Intention]</span> 
- Seeks medically accurate information on the health risks of daily hamburger consumption. 
- Wants personalized dietary advice focused on reducing ultra-processed foods. 
- Aims to gain knowledge to make self-directed dietary changes. 
<span id="A4.T15.2.6.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Implicit Intention]</span> 
- Desires reassurance to alleviate anxiety regarding his eating habits. 
- Wants to feel more in control of his health and lifestyle choices.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Cases of events and sub-intentions in LifeSim-Eval</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F29" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.12152v1/theme_dis.svg" id="A4.F29.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:381/320;" width="381" height="320"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 29: </span>Distribution of all the event-desire pair in LifeSim-Eval. Each point represent a keyword from event-desire pair.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each scenario, we give the details of each metric:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intent Recognition</span> evaluates whether the assistant can accurately infer the user’s underlying intentions throughout an interaction episode. For each scenario, we construct an intention checklist <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{|\mathcal{I}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{|\mathcal{I}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{I}|\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{I}|\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, containing both explicit and implicit intentions. Prior to generating each assistant response at turn <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the model predicts the user’s current intention <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. All predicted intentions across the episode are aggregated into a set <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{I}}=\bigcup_{t}\hat{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{I}}=\bigcup_{t}\hat{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and compared against the gold checklist <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> using an LLM-based evaluator. For each intention <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, a binary indicator <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(i_{k})\in{0,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(i_{k})\in{0,1}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned, where <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(i_{k})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(i_{k})=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is correctly identified by the model and 0 otherwise. The final intent recognition accuracy is then computed as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}|}\sum_{i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}}s(i_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}|}\sum_{i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}}s(i_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and averaged across all scenarios. We partition the intention checklist into an explicit intent set <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and an implicit intent set <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and report intent recognition accuracy separately as <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intent Completion</span> evaluates whether the assistant ultimately fulfills the user’s explicit and implicit intentions over a multi-turn interaction. Given the predefined intention checklist <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}={i_{1},\ldots,i_{|\mathcal{I}|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}={i_{1},\ldots,i_{|\mathcal{I}|}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we assess whether each intention <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is successfully satisfied by the assistant’s responses. An LLM-based evaluator assigns a binary completion indicator <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(i_{k})\in{0,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(i_{k})\in{0,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(i_{k})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(i_{k})=1</annotation></semantics></math> if the intention is adequately fulfilled in the dialogue and 0 otherwise. The intent completion score is computed as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{R}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}|}\sum_{i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}}c(i_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{R}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}|}\sum_{i_{k}\in\mathcal{I}}c(i_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the final metric is obtained by averaging <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{R}</annotation></semantics></math> across all episodes. Analogously, we report intent completion performance separately for the explicit and implicit intent sets, denoted as <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{R}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{R}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{R}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{R}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Naturalness</span> assesses whether the assistant’s responses conform to human conversational norms, demonstrating fluent, contextually appropriate, and stylistically natural language use.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coherence</span> measures the semantic and logical consistency of the assistant’s utterances across turns, ensuring that the dialogue remains contextually grounded and free from internal contradictions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Preference Recovery</span> evaluates the model’s ability to infer stable user preferences. For each scenario, the assistant predicts a preference vector <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{p}}=\{\hat{p}^{(d)}\}_{d=1}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{p}}=\{\hat{p}^{(d)}\}_{d=1}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> preference dimensions, where each dimension takes a discrete value in <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\text{low},\text{high}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>low</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>high</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\text{low},\text{high}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A prediction is considered correct if <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{(d)}=p^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{(d)}=p^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The preference recovery accuracy is computed as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{A}_{\text{pref}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}|}\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{I}\left[\hat{p}^{(d)}=p^{(d)}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}_{\text{pref}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}|}\sum_{d\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{I}\left[\hat{p}^{(d)}=p^{(d)}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and averaged across all scenarios.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Persona Alignment</span> examines the degree to which the assistant’s responses remain faithful to the user’s predefined persona or profile, reflecting the model’s ability to incorporate and consistently respect enduring user characteristics throughout the interaction.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure  <a href="#A4.F30" title="Figure 30 ‣ Metrics ‣ Appendix D LifeSim-Eval Details ‣ LifeSim: Long-Horizon User Life Simulator for Personalized Assistant Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>, <a href="#A4.F31" title="Figure 31 ‣ Metrics ‣ Appendix D LifeSim-Eval Details ‣ LifeSim: Long-Horizon User Life Simulator for Personalized Assistant Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, <a href="#A4.F32" title="Figure 32 ‣ Metrics ‣ Appendix D LifeSim-Eval Details ‣ LifeSim: Long-Horizon User Life Simulator for Personalized Assistant Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, <a href="#A4.F33" title="Figure 33 ‣ Metrics ‣ Appendix D LifeSim-Eval Details ‣ LifeSim: Long-Horizon User Life Simulator for Personalized Assistant Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.F34" title="Figure 34 ‣ Metrics ‣ Appendix D LifeSim-Eval Details ‣ LifeSim: Long-Horizon User Life Simulator for Personalized Assistant Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> show prompts for LifeSim-Eval.</p>
</div>
